  "summary": "The audit checks the 45 graduate units, the three core courses (HISTORY 371, ANTHRO 319, EDUC 327), the LATINAM 200 seminar in each of three quarters and LATINAM 397A and 397B, 10 units of related courses (at most 3 units of LATINAM 300), 5 advisor-approved elective units you move in, LATINAM 398 (only 1 unit counts) and a three-course language sequence. Every course must be letter graded with B- or better, numbered 100 or above, with at least half the units at the 200 level. Checked by hand: the 3.0 GPA, the capstone or thesis paper, Law and GSB courses (exempt from letter grades but held to a B- equivalent), and whether language units count toward the 45: the Bulletin says both \"including\" and \"excluding\" the language requirement. External credit is not accepted.",
